# The characters of the game's font, by code: four hexadecimal digits, then the character. Codes
# 0100-08FF are glyphs. Latin letters, digits and punctuation are full-width forms: the game draws
# every glyph in the same cell. A code with no line is written {K:xxxx} in a script.
# Blank glyphs: 0134 04D3 04D4 04D5 04D6 04D7 04FB 04FC 04FD 04FE 04FF 051E 051F 057E 057F 058E 058F
# 059F 062F 069F 06FF 073F 07AF 07B2 07C4 07C7 07EF. 04D7, which the byte 20 stands for, is the one the
# script puts between words, and is a full-width space here.
# 04F9 and 0795 both draw ｖ.
